# Ignored modernization suggestions
# Format: <date> <category> <description>
2026-05-24 t-context internal/server/server_test.go:86 shutdown() helper is called from t.Cleanup blocks (api_e2e_test.go:45,199) where t.Context() is already canceled — using it would defeat apiServer.Shutdown's graceful drain. context.Background() with explicit 5s timeout is intentional.
2026-07-31 cmp-or internal/config/config.go:175 applyZeroValueDefaults keeps explicit `if x == 0` blocks rather than cmp.Or. The comments there distinguish zero ("use the default") from negative ("no read timeout", preserved deliberately) — semantics cmp.Or would obscure. MaxConnections tests `< 0`, not a zero value, so it cannot use cmp.Or at all.
2026-08-20 complit-fold internal/eventlog/eventlog_test.go:287 TestConfigureReplacesPreviousSink keeps `base.FilePath = first` as its own statement instead of folding it into the Settings literal. `go fix -diff` suggests the fold; golangci-lint's modernize does not. `base` is a template mutated across the test and the next step is `base.FilePath = second`, so the separate assignment is what makes "this is the field that varies" legible. Applying modernizer output mechanically is also how a duplicate-key literal reached internal/logshell/nested.go and stopped the tree compiling.
